+        /*
+         * Close the read with a bare envelope -- no payload, the request's own
+         * sequence -- which is the shape every other service here already
+         * answers with. Stock sends one per read: four of them on this service
+         * in its boot capture (sequences 6, 7, 7, 9) against three file reads,
+         * and we sent none.
+         *
+         * Without it the CP never treats a read as finished and asks again,
+         * about twice a second, for as long as it is up. Matching the frame
+         * size, the payload shape, the block size and even the file's bytes to
+         * stock changed nothing; this was the one thing left that stock does
+         * and we did not.
+         */
+        frames.push(
+            GipcMessage {
+                r#type: Some(TYPE_RESPONSE),
+                endpoint: req.endpoint,
+                service: req.service,
+                method: req.method,
+                payload: None,
+                sequence: req.sequence,
+            }
+            .encode_to_vec(),
+        );
         eprintln!(
